+# Fixed reviewed-source Linux package candidate
+
+The target is **dd59817f750684b093965f539dd4de466be13077**, directly reviewed by genuine evidence child **c2b146adb6d03814f2bd9a7af72baf003bb48812**. It has tree6a9a08af70fb94b50ed2b5eee6aaf3686f648b99 and webc516655efaac8260b1bcf5938f8f4d65ab61ad44. The later merge5189547f76bf24c002b8e8b11669081ba67ad2c6 has the same tree; this workflow does not rename the direct-child attestation as an attestation of that merge or of this builder branch.
+
+The existing artifact workflow381238005 has two runs,38138212902 and38192054066. Its current fixed source is old8bcd. The retained8bcd archive and manifest remain unchanged. A bounded local receipt search and the complete two-run history of that known workflow found no dd package; this is not a universal absence claim about arbitrary other workflows. Before triggering this candidate, check again for an existing successful same-target receipt and avoid duplicate builds.
+
+This new workflow uses the existing pinned checkout/setup-node/upload actions and Node22.14. It first checks out the actual event subject and installs that subject's exact locks, then executes the original canonical product-correctness command. The complete log/TAP, all155 passing cases and31 distinct named PCR cases, execution commit/full tree/web tree, actual lock hashes and workflow/trigger/run identities are recorded in builder-correctness.json. This is a new execution required by the workflow; no hosted result is claimed before it runs. The original source-led ordinary workflow paths do not cover this new workflow, so this fresh test stage is explicit here. Protected workflows, their trust policy and their paths are unchanged.
+
+Only after that stage succeeds does a second pinned checkout retrieve c2b with full history, remove the builder working tree/dependencies and detach to dd. It checks both exact approved trees and clean source, then uses the unchanged runtime-release resolver and installs dd's own locks. Source/packager both remain dd. Receipts outside the workspace retain both subjects separately: builder155/PCR31 is not application-dd testing, and dd's build/browser/package results are not builder testing. The export records the builder workflow/trigger identities separately. No input can choose a different artifact source, approval, root or deploy target. Permissions are contents:read; there are no secrets, production credentials, database calls, migration, deployment or approval issuance.
+
+Calculation/package/type/lint/build and the existing development-only trade-plan browser suite run sequentially on a fresh Ubuntu job. That browser suite starts a dev fixture server; its result must not be called packaged production verification. A separate probe starts the actual packaged server.js with NODE_ENV=production, an explicit minimal credential-free child environment and loopback binding. It checks the exact missing-auth configuration response, production fixture404 and a served static member matching the package manifest SHA. A500 auth rejection is expected fail-closed behavior, **not healthy production readiness**. Confirmed child shutdown is required. No synthetic production token or fixture-enabling production flag is supplied.
+
+The original packager and verifier bind all release members and reject forbidden files. SHA256SUMS covers the new archive, manifest, verification, source/review provenance, separate builder-canonical receipts and packaged boot receipts. No local Mac build, hosted build or browser/native run has been performed for this candidate yet. It needs independent workflow review, ordinary hosted execution and normal protected release gates. Do not dispatch it while another owned heavy task is active; do not rerun an already successful same-target package. This clean release assembly carries only the workflow and this handoff; historical8dd/ae1e candidates and their raw static evidence remain on codex/reviewed-publication-tail-artifact-oct14.
+
+The upload step also retains any available partial receipts from a failed job, and its artifact name includes the actual job status. Such partial output is diagnostic evidence only. A valid release package requires a successful complete job, the full archive/verifier/boot receipts and matching SHA256SUMS; an uploaded failure artifact does not establish packaging or readiness.
+
+The package is application/runtime release preparation. It does not install the financial50 or publication26 SQL, enable the unfinished versioned-input protocol, establish fixed private peer transport, qualify sources/articles or grant strategy authority. Last read-only production observation at2026-10-14T12:14:19Z still points to169aad1b6cfa747f78ae3464b614f43c0749d806. Available15967711232 is below the unchanged19998441472 binary guard by4030730240bytes. No heavy admission or deployment was attempted, reserves were not lowered, and the existing capacity decision was not re-asked.
